% Raga melodies from A. H. Fox Strangways, The Music of Hindostan (Oxford:
% Clarendon Press, 1914), chapter XI, "Specimens of Rags", pp. 301-311: songs
% from the books of the Poona Gayan Samaj (singing school), which Fox
% Strangways printed in staff notation. The book is in the public domain
% everywhere (the author died in 1948; US publication 1914). Scan:
% https://archive.org/details/musicofhindostan00foxs (page = printed page + 48).
%
% A first reading from the scan, 2026-11-09, to be checked against the plates:
% the pitches and rhythms were read from the engraving at high magnification,
% and the bars marked "check" in the notes came out short or long. Asthayi and
% antara (the two sections) are separated by a double bar as in the book.
% Sa is C in every tune, as Fox Strangways wrote them. Each tune carries a
% %%tuning line with the raga's own notes in cents, taken from the 22-sruti
% table the joyboard carries (just thirds and sixths at 386 and 884, komal
% re ga dha ni at 112, 316, 814 and 996, shuddha Ni at 1088); map=nearest
% puts each written note on its sruti. The tala is named in R: and the metre
% written as Fox Strangways barred it: Eka Trisra as 3/4, Rupak as a bar of
% six quavers.

X:1
T:Bhup
T:Bhupali, Rupak
C:traditional (Poona Gayan Samaj)
O:India, Hindustani
R:Rupak
S:Fox Strangways, The Music of Hindostan (1914), Ex. 383, p. 301
N:Pentatonic (Sa Re Ga Pa Dha). Check: the last bar has four quavers in the plate.
M:3/4
L:1/8
K:C
%%style drone
E | GE D3 E | C2 C2 E2 | A,A, C3 E | D2 E D2 E | GE D3 E |
C2 C2 E2 | A,A, C3 E | GE DE z E || ED E3 E | cG c2 cc |
cG c3 c | d2 c2 GA | E2 D2 C2 | E2 D2 A,G, | A,2 C3 E | EG DE |]
%%tuning Bhup (Sa Re Ga Pa Dha): 203.9 386.3 702.0 884.4 2/1 map=nearest

X:2
T:Malkos
T:Malkauns, Eka Trisra, slow
C:traditional (Poona Gayan Samaj)
O:India, Hindustani
R:Eka Trisra
S:Fox Strangways, The Music of Hindostan (1914), Ex. 407, p. 308
N:Pentatonic with komal Ga, Dha and Ni (Sa ga ma dha ni). Check: bar 5 and bar 9.
M:3/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=66
K:Cm
%%style drone
C | E2 C C2 C | C3 CA,C | C3 E2 E | E2 E C2 C | E2 A, A,2 A, |
C3 CA,C | C3 E2 E | E2 E C2 C | E3 E2 F || B2 c c2 c | c2 c c2 c |
c/c/B/c/ AF F2 | FE C C2 C | C3 CA,C | C3 E2 E | E2 E C2 |]
%%tuning Malkos (Sa ga ma dha ni): 315.6 498.0 813.7 996.1 2/1 map=nearest

X:3
T:Bhairavi
T:Bhairavi, Eka Trisra, slow
C:traditional (Poona Gayan Samaj)
O:India, Hindustani
R:Eka Trisra
S:Fox Strangways, The Music of Hindostan (1914), Ex. 419, p. 311
N:All four komal notes (re ga dha ni); Fox Strangways heads it Phrygian-Doric. Check: bars 4, 7 and 9 are short in this reading.
M:3/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=66
K:Cphr
%%style drone
C | F3 F2 F | E3 E2 E | D3 D2 D | C2 D | D2 D z z C | D3 D2 E |
ED DC C | C3 E2 F | ED CC F || F3 A2 c | c2 c c2 c | c2 c c2 d |
cB A F2 F | F3 F2 A | AF F D2 D | C3 D2 E | EDC C2 |]
%%tuning Bhairavi (Sa re ga ma Pa dha ni): 111.7 315.6 498.0 702.0 813.7 996.1 2/1 map=nearest

X:4
T:Desh
T:Desh, Eka Trisra, slow
C:traditional (Poona Gayan Samaj)
O:India, Hindustani
R:Eka Trisra
S:Fox Strangways, The Music of Hindostan (1914), Ex. 395, p. 305
N:Both nishads: shuddha Ni (B natural) rising, komal ni (B flat) falling. The asthayi repeats. Check: bars 6 and 7.
M:3/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=66
K:Cmix
%%style drone
D2 D F2 A | =Bc c c2 _B | AG AFGA | G2 DED z :|
D2 D F2 A | =Bc c c2 c | c2 c2 c=B | cd c d3 |
c =B2 c2 d | dc c2 AF | AG AFGA | G2 DEDD |]
%%tuning Desh (Sa Re Ga ma Pa Dha ni Ni): 203.9 386.3 498.0 702.0 884.4 996.1 1088.3 2/1 map=nearest
